    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
    "body": "What are your thoughts about automatically updating the `'` bookmark with the position right before someone jumps to a bookmark? Here is one use case. Let's say I want to copy a bunch of non-consecutive files to the same target location. With this feature, I can mark the destination directory with a bookmark, let's assume I use `d`. Then I go to the source directory, perform my yank, press `'d`, paste, then press `''` to immediately jump back, and then repeat the process but this time without ever needing to press `'d` again as I can just just use `''` to jump back and forth now.",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">What are your thoughts about automatically updating the <code class=\"notranslate\">'</code> bookmark with the position right before someone jumps to a bookmark? Here is one use case. Let's say I want to copy a bunch of non-consecutive files to the same target location. With this feature, I can mark the destination directory with a bookmark, let's assume I use <code class=\"notranslate\">d</code>. Then I go to the source directory, perform my yank, press <code class=\"notranslate\">'d</code>, paste, then press <code class=\"notranslate\">''</code> to immediately jump back, and then repeat the process but this time without ever needing to press <code class=\"notranslate\">'d</code> again as I can just just use <code class=\"notranslate\">''</code> to jump back and forth now.</p>",
    "bodyText": "What are your thoughts about automatically updating the ' bookmark with the position right before someone jumps to a bookmark? Here is one use case. Let's say I want to copy a bunch of non-consecutive files to the same target location. With this feature, I can mark the destination directory with a bookmark, let's assume I use d. Then I go to the source directory, perform my yank, press 'd, paste, then press '' to immediately jump back, and then repeat the process but this time without ever needing to press 'd again as I can just just use '' to jump back and forth now.",
