    "comment_count": 2,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nYes, I've considered that. I *barely* convinced myself that adding the whole built-in bookmarks was worth adding 100 lines to 'mini.files' file. And implementing this behavior would lead to even more, while it can be reproduced with deliberate `m'` prior to jumping.\r\n\r\n**However**, I somehow missed the possibility of setting this bookmark *before every jump* (in my mind it was something more complicated like automated tracking of \"latest visited directory\" or something). Setting it just before performing a jump is only essentially +3 lines. I'll think about it.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for the suggestion!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, I've considered that. I <em>barely</em> convinced myself that adding the whole built-in bookmarks was worth adding 100 lines to 'mini.files' file. And implementing this behavior would lead to even more, while it can be reproduced with deliberate <code class=\"notranslate\">m'</code> prior to jumping.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>However</strong>, I somehow missed the possibility of setting this bookmark <em>before every jump</em> (in my mind it was something more complicated like automated tracking of \"latest visited directory\" or something). Setting it just before performing a jump is only essentially +3 lines. I'll think about it.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Thanks for the suggestion!\nYes, I've considered that. I barely convinced myself that adding the whole built-in bookmarks was worth adding 100 lines to 'mini.files' file. And implementing this behavior would lead to even more, while it can be reproduced with deliberate m' prior to jumping.\nHowever, I somehow missed the possibility of setting this bookmark before every jump (in my mind it was something more complicated like automated tracking of \"latest visited directory\" or something). Setting it just before performing a jump is only essentially +3 lines. I'll think about it.",
